{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.CountingModuliGrade","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.CountingModuliGrade","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Information.SurrealBudgetGrade"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.not_familyPolyBounded_decision_of_bridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.not_familyPolyBounded_decision_of_bridge","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CountingModuliGrade.lean#L141-L149","doc":"**Conditional consequence (sorry-free): given the decision-hardness bridge,\nno uniform polynomial *decision* algorithm over the moduli space.**  A\nrigorous *conditional* statement — everything is proved modulo the single\nopen class instance, which is the actual `P≠NP` content and stays absent.\nContrast `not_familyPolyBounded_of_physical_point`, which needs no bridge:\nthat is the counting axis (proved); this is the decision axis (open). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.PhotonicDecisionHard.hard_point","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.PhotonicDecisionHard.hard_point","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CountingModuliGrade.lean#L139-L139","doc":"Some moduli point is decision-ω-super-polynomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.PhotonicDecisionHard.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.PhotonicDecisionHard.mk","kind":"ctor","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CountingModuliGrade.lean#L137-L137","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.PhotonicDecisionHard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.PhotonicDecisionHard","kind":"class","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CountingModuliGrade.lean#L129-L139","doc":"**Photonic–Turing DECISION hardness (conjecture; NO instance — the wall).**\nThe counting-axis result above is unconditional; crossing to the *decision*\naxis is `res ≠ 0 ⟹ P≠NP`.  This class carries the open content: some moduli\npoint's **decision** cost (not merely its counting cost) is\nω-super-polynomial.  An instance would exhibit a decision-hard problem =\nprove `P≠NP` (indeed a super-polynomial *general* — not merely\nbandwidth-limited — lower bound); it stays **absent** (anti-laundering:\naxiomatization is not proof). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.PhotonicEncoding.charges","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.PhotonicEncoding.charges","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CountingModuliGrade.lean#L127-L127","doc":"The moduli point charges at least the machine's cost (Bekenstein reading). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.PhotonicEncoding.machineCost","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.PhotonicEncoding.machineCost","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CountingModuliGrade.lean#L125-L125","doc":"The machine's intrinsic counting cost. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.PhotonicEncoding.encode","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.PhotonicEncoding.encode","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CountingModuliGrade.lean#L123-L123","doc":"Machine/problem index ↦ its photonic initial condition (a moduli point). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.PhotonicEncoding.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.PhotonicEncoding.mk","kind":"ctor","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CountingModuliGrade.lean#L121-L121","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.PhotonicEncoding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.PhotonicEncoding","kind":"structure","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CountingModuliGrade.lean#L113-L127","doc":"**Photonic encoding of computation (data, not a claim).**  The QOU\ndictionary *\"initial photonic condition = Turing state\"* as a structure: a\nmap `encode` from a machine/problem index to a moduli point (the photonic\ninitial condition realizing that machine's configuration), and the\nmachine's own counting cost `machineCost`.  The coherence field records\nthat the moduli point charges (at least) the machine's cost — this is the\nBekenstein/physical reading, structural not fitted.  Providing this is\n*naming the dictionary*; it makes **no** complexity claim by itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.not_familyPolyBounded_of_physical_point","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.not_familyPolyBounded_of_physical_point","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CountingModuliGrade.lean#L102-L109","doc":"**No uniform polynomial counting over the QOU moduli space (sorry-free,\nunconditional).**  Because the boundary family occupies a hard-stratum\npoint, the moduli space of QOU counting problems admits **no** single\npolynomial-time counting algorithm.  This is the proved *counting-axis*\nstatement — the `#P`-over-moduli result. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.physical_point_hard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.physical_point_hard","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CountingModuliGrade.lean#L94-L100","doc":"**The boundary moduli point is in the hard stratum (sorry-free).**  Any cost\nfamily whose fiber at `m` is the physical boundary cost has `m` in its hard\nstratum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.physicalCost_superPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.physicalCost_superPoly","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CountingModuliGrade.lean#L87-L92","doc":"**The physical cost is ω-super-polynomial (sorry-free, unconditional).**\nDirectly from `qou_physical_intractability_unconditional` at bandwidth\n`B = 1`: the `3^{3n}` tree dominates every polynomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.physicalCost","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.physicalCost","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CountingModuliGrade.lean#L81-L85","doc":"**The physical counting cost** of the QOU boundary family: the surviving\n`3^{3n}`-leaf skein resolution tree (non-torsion regime, nothing cancels),\nread by a unit-bandwidth device.  This is the counting cost `#P` actually\ncharges at the boundary moduli point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.not_familyPolyBounded_of_hardStratum_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.not_familyPolyBounded_of_hardStratum_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CountingModuliGrade.lean#L74-L77","doc":"**Nonempty hard stratum ⟹ no uniform poly bound (sorry-free).** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.not_familyPolyBounded_of_hardPoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.not_familyPolyBounded_of_hardPoint","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CountingModuliGrade.lean#L65-L72","doc":"**A single hard point kills every uniform poly bound (sorry-free).**  One\nω-super-polynomial moduli point suffices: no `c·nᵏ` can dominate the family,\nbecause it would have to dominate that point's super-polynomial fiber.  This\nis the moduli form of the surreal squeeze — the hard stratum obstructs\nuniform polynomial counting. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.polyBounded_fiber_of_familyPolyBounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.polyBounded_fiber_of_familyPolyBounded","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CountingModuliGrade.lean#L57-L63","doc":"**A uniform bound restricts to every fiber (sorry-free).**  If one\npolynomial dominates the family, it dominates each single-moduli-point cost\nfunction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.HardStratum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.HardStratum","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CountingModuliGrade.lean#L52-L55","doc":"**The hard stratum** of a cost family: the moduli points whose counting\ncost is ω-super-polynomial.  The surreal grade stratifies `M` into the\npoly-cost locus and this hard locus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.FamilyPolyBounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.FamilyPolyBounded","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/CountingModuliGrade.lean#L47-L50","doc":"**Uniform polynomial bound over the whole moduli space** — one algorithm,\nevery problem: a single `c·nᵏ` dominates `cost m n` at *every* moduli point\n`m`.  This is the `P`-style \"polynomial for all instances\" hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0}]}